    {
      "id": "f4896f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 7,
      "content": "Transfer students may satisfy General Education requirements by completing the California General Education Transfer Curriculum (Cal-GETC), or by completing an Associate Degree for Transfer (AA-T/AS-T) . Transfer students are advised to take courses required for their major as part General Education, as specified by each major, to achieve the minimum units to degree. Major courses and campus-wide required courses that are approved for GE credit shall also fulfill (double count for) the GE requirement. [ EO 1100 ] For more information regarding Associate Degree for Transfer, please see your California community college counselor or visit: www.adegreewithaguarantee.com/",
      "contentHtml": "<p>Transfer students may satisfy General Education requirements by completing the California General Education Transfer Curriculum (Cal-GETC), or by completing an <a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/apply/transfer/Pages/ccc-associate-degree-for-transfer.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Associate Degree for Transfer (AA-T/AS-T)</a>.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Transfer students are advised to take courses required for their major as part General Education, as specified by each major, to achieve the minimum units to degree.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Major courses and campus-wide required courses that are approved for GE credit shall also fulfill (double count for) the GE requirement. [<a href=\"https://calstate.policystat.com/policy/6741976/latest/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">EO 1100</a>]</p><p><br></p><p>For more information regarding Associate Degree for Transfer, please see your California community college counselor or visit: <a href=\"http://www.adegreewithaguarantee.com/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">www.adegreewithaguarantee.com/</a></p>"
    }
